  "details": "Recently I started development of a game within VRC that utilizes Unity’s built in nav mesh generation (Specifically 2022.3.6f1) However, I have since discovered that these nav meshes don’t work at all in game, but work okay in the emulator. Udon# code related to a nav mesh agent works, but having a script of any kind trying to access the nav mesh surface will cause it to completely break.\n\nThis is the script I made:\n\nusing UdonSharp;\n\nusing UnityEngine.AI;\n\nusing Unity.AI.Navigation;\n\nusing UnityEngine;\n\nusing VRC.SDKBase;\n\nusing VRC.Udon;\n\npublic class test : UdonSharpBehaviour\n\n{\n\n    public NavMeshSurface NavMeshSurfaceTest;\n\n}\n\nEven with a script as simple as this causes Unity to spew a series of errors. Udon# simply does not support nav mesh surfaces but supports nav mesh agents(???). As if this issue isn’t stupid enough as it is, Hilariously, It seems to work perfectly fine in older versions of unity (2019.4.31f1). I can’t even fathom how ridiculous it is that this is even a problem in the first place. Maybe stop hosting stupid events that no one cares about and fix your broken game. The community has put up with enough garbage as it is.\n\nSincerely,\n\nA frustrated game developer using your garbage system",
